Spoilers may lie ahead - read at your own risk!

So, after ascending a Valkyrie, I did many experiments with different 
kinds of characters - Wizards, Priests, Monks, Tourists - but without 
success. A while ago I started trying to play archeologists, much 
because of the possibility to sell gems early for lots of money to donate.

This character had a pretty lucky start. He found a +2 oilskin cloak 
lying around in DLVL 2 and a magic lamp in minetown, although his pet 
died very early. Minetown temple was also co-aligned. I sacfested until 
I got what I wanted - a silver saber named Grayswandir. A large scroll 
shop was found in DLVL 5 which yielded some echant weapon and armor 
scrolls, a spellbook of identify (I can cast it now with 4% failure!), 
and maybe the most important thing, a scroll of genocide (you will find 
the reason for this below). I spent the magic lamp on a gray dragon 
scale mail (maybe silver would have been a better choice!).

So, after doing Sokoban for the BoH, I started going down. Right below 
the rogue level was a hearse bones file, and there I met an 
arch-lich(!!). I decided to try how hard those are, but it was able to 
heal faster than I did damage with my (at that moment +0) Grayswandir. 
After a couple of cursed items i decided to engrave Elbereth at the 
stairs with a wand of digging. That didn't help either, the purple L 
kept summoning annoying monsters such as umber hulks and a minotaur who 
did not care about the engraving. At this part I fled and identified all 
scrolls in the scroll store and found the scroll of genocide, which I 
promptly blessed and used to get rid of Ls.

Medusa had a peaceful titan. I still lacked any forms of levitation 
(excluding some potions of levitation), so I decided to dig down. But 
before doing that, I used a magic trap to tame the titan (he's still a 
pet of mine). I found a pair of levitation boots somewhere, and 2 
shields of reflection. Castle wasn't too hard with +6 Grayswandir at 
expert. I also found a silver saber and boots of speed there. The wand 
was just at 0:1, and I used the first wish for a blessed magic marker. I 
had a ?ofCharging at my base, so I went back there. I used the 3 wishes 
for 2 more magic markers and gauntlets of dexterity.

The quest was a piece of cake with AC -34 (-41 with [oReflecction) - in 
the quest nemesis level I tried to teleport somewhere, and ended right 
next to my meditating quest nemesis! Two hits from Grayswandir were 
enough. I returned later to grab all the loots, and I found yet another 
magic lamp!

At one moment I was at my stash, and found an unidentified potion - 
identified it as a potion of polymorph! I decided to try dipping a spare 
unicorn horn for the small chance of something good - and I got a magic 
marker at 1:63! :)

So this is where I am now. I have two wishes, but no idea what I should 
use them to - maybe I will save one for an emergency.

